{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>ויקחו לי תרומה</b> — 'Speak to the children of Israel' opens with conciliatory language, like 'speak to the heart of Jerusalem.' Because it involved financial burden, He placated them. In the Midrash: Rabbi Abbahu said — and what of making a Tabernacle of glory and atonement for Israel? 'Speak to the children of Israel' — conciliatory language. Those who press Israel and take their money — what shall be upon them? תרומה. Letters of מ' תורה — for the Torah given over מ' days belongs to eaters of תרומה. As we say: the Torah was given only to eaters of the manna; paired to eaters of תרומה. This is 'ויקחו לי' — for My name; whoever engages in Torah is as if he takes for Me, for the Holy One, blessed be He, has in the world only four cubits of halakhah alone. Therefore He juxtaposed the pericope of ויקחו לי תרומה to the pericope of Torah." "<b>ויקחו לי תרומה</b> — Make Me one sanctuary place from the 50 of the Temple Mount, like תרומה which is 1 from 50. For the Temple Mount was 500 by 500, and the place of the courtyard was 100 by 50, which is 1 from 50 of 500 by 500. He juxtaposed וילך to ויקחו לי תרומה — hinting the time of eating תרומה at night, as we learned: 'From when the priests enter to eat their תרומה' — which is the emergence of the stars." "<b>ויקחו לי</b> — לי עולה מ' — this is a generous eye, 1 from מ'." "<b>מאת כל</b> — כל עולה נ' — this is a middling one, 1 from נ'." "<b>מאת כל</b> — ר\"ת עולה ס' — this is an evil eye, 1 from ס'." "<b>אל בני ישראל ויקחו לי תרומה</b> — in gematria: אך בני ישראל יהיו תורמין — only the children of Israel shall bring תרומה, not the nations." "<b>תקחו את תרומתי</b> — and He did not say תקח, for charity is not collected from fewer than 2. תקחו — in gematria: שנים קחו — two shall take."], :book :exodus, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {1 "Resolved וילך (Deut 31:1) as the preceding pericope ending, which Ba'al HaTurim reads as לילה by notarikon or association; the text reads 'סמך לילה' which I render as the juxtaposition hinting night."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:14:26.424103178Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}